{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1340810-c5-ruminations","id":1340810,"title":"C5 ruminations","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-10-11T11:30:42-07:00","id":1340810,"title":"C5 ruminations","content":"Having played V5, I feel that they did a great job streamlining the experience of playing Vampire and making it more narrative/story focused than number crunchy. They made the mechanics reflect the themes that were only really implied before. So my question is, what do you think will carry over to a new edition of Changeling (if they make one)? <br /> <br /> Some of the big changes I would note are the combat, damage, attributes, Willpower, complete removal of Freebies, Difficulty rolls, Character trait template allocation, hunger and predator types. I think most of these are great (kind of neither here nor there on the new combat and Willpower being tied to attributes tbh). Obviously Hunger and Predator types are not applicable, but predator types could be translated to a new form of Thresholds. If the Hunger bar indicates anything, Nightmare/Glamour/Banality will likely get a massive overhaul (which I actually think they need). What form could this take? A lot of this translates well, but a lot of it is also pretty complex. I love what V5 did for Vampire, and I frankly would like to start house ruling a good bit of it to Changeling, provided my players were a bit more experienced with the subject. I dont necessarily have specific questions, I just think this is an interesting topic and wanted to hear peoples thoughts on what they might carry over/how they might do it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25663-rigelj","name":"RigelJ","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-11T11:51:31-07:00","id":1340816,"title":"","content":"On a cheeky note I feel my ruminations would be &quot;Why call it C5? Wouldn't C4 be more appropriate?&quot; Unlike Vampire Changeling only has 3 previous editions. First published 1995. Second published 1997. C20 published 2017.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9015-zee-patrick","name":"zee PaTrick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-11T13:51:59-07:00","id":1340835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zee PaTrick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1340810-c5-ruminations?p=1340816#post1340816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a cheeky note I feel my ruminations would be &amp;quot;Why call it C5? Wouldn't C4 be more appropriate?&amp;quot; Unlike Vampire Changeling only has 3 previous editions. First published 1995. Second published 1997. C20 published 2017.</div> </div> </div> </div>A fair point, though I have only gotten into WoD in the last 2 years. I started with the 20th anniversary editions, my knowledge is quite limited past that","signature":"","edited":{"use