:"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-12T06:00:27-07:00","id":1340934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1340810-c5-ruminations?p=1340890#post1340890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">its ok! Assuming the Schedual stays on track you have until 2030!</div> </div> </div> </div>Hahahahaha! This is purely as a fan who really enjoys the V5 system. Like you said, it\u2019ll be quite a while before anyone starts thinking about something official.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-12T09:49:53-07:00","id":1340964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1340810-c5-ruminations?p=1340934#post1340934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hahahahaha! This is purely as a fan who really enjoys the V5 system. Like you said, it\u2019ll be quite a while before anyone starts thinking about something official.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm of Two minds.. I'd like to see more c20, but also would like to see a more extreme revision. But that we haven't even seen anything looking like plans for other 5e WOD does make me imagine its pretty far our. Especially I think we saw v5 two years early? I know Ww20 has been stopped for the idea that Ww5 be worked on but.. that's all. M20 has at least two books still being developed so.. who knows?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-12T11:26:31-07:00","id":1340976,"title":"","content":"Who knows indeed! We\u2019d all love to work on more C20 books, but no one\u2019s given the green light.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-13T19:59:55-07:00","id":1341203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1340810-c5-ruminations?p=1340858#post1340858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have lots of thoughts on this. I\u2019m not quite ready to share them yet though. Soon!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Its rude to tease. (;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25663,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25663-rigelj","user":"RigelJ","date":". 10-14-2019, 01:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25663-rigelj","name":"RigelJ","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T19:53:34-07:00","id":1345148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RigelJ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1340810-c5-ruminations?p=1341203#post1341203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its rude to tease. (;</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right, but now it's Samhain, so the teasing is over. The faeries are out to play! Here's my conversion guide for Changeling: The Dreaming into 5th Edition World of Darkness: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1XCSfDfJUNFm6d9f0omHzQ-rt7U0kkR7b/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/1XCS...ew?usp=sharing</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T18:00:24-08:00","id":1346326,"title":"","content":"Are tithed basically Lost?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T19:24:16-08:00","id":1346330,"title":"","content":"They\u2019re originally from the Time of Judgement book, but yeah, they\u2019re Lost if the the Lost were the scary bad guys.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T08:25:39-08:00","id":1346458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1340810-c5-ruminations?p=1345148#post1345148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're right, but now it's Samhain, so the teasing is over. The faeries are out to play! Here's my conversion guide for Changeling: The Dreaming into 5th Edition World of Darkness: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1XCSfDfJUNFm6d9f0omHzQ-rt7U0kkR7b/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/1XCS...ew?usp=sharing</a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> MY DUDE WAY TO WAKE ME THE HELL UP<br /> <br /> What am I looking at? Is this... a preview? I see its a conversion guide, is this all we're going to get, or is this a taste of whats to come? If you can say","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25663-rigelj","name":"RigelJ","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T09:08:28-08:00","id":1346472,"title":"","content":"I AM RIDING THE HYPE TRAIN ON THIS, FULL STEAM AHEAD, CHOO CHOO MOTHERF*CKERS","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25663-rigelj","name":"RigelJ","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T09:24:12-08:00","id":1346479,"title":"","content":"Hahahahaha! As much as I'd love to work on whatever official form Changeling takes in 5th edition World of Darkness, this is purely a fan work on my part. I thought Changeling would be a great fit for the V5 system, so this little conversion guide was born.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T09:51:20-08:00","id":1346491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1340810-c5-ruminations?p=1346479#post1346479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hahahahaha! As much as I'd love to work on whatever official form Changeling takes in 5th edition World of Darkness, this is purely a fan work on my part. I thought Changeling would be a great fit for the V5 system, so this little conversion guide was born.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahh, I appear to have misunderstood. I thought this was slightly more official, and was confused as to why I could not find it anywhere else. I agree with your stance on Nightmare/Banality being very V5 compatible, Im just at a loss for what to do with it. My players are only just getting into changeling, and while I have read both C20 and V5 cover to cover, none of them have read either. I think they'd be too intimidated by the prospect have having to READ to actually partake in a sort of 3 core book combo game. So, given that this is all you, may I ask a few questions on it? Theres a few areas that are a little confusing to me.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25663-rigelj","name":"RigelJ","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T09:53:07-08:00","id":1346492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1340810-c5-ruminations?p=1346479#post1346479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hahahahaha! As much as I'd love to work on whatever official form Changeling takes in 5th edition World of Darkness, this is purely a fan work on my part. I thought Changeling would be a great fit for the V5 system, so this little conversion guide was born.</div> </div> </div> </div>also, would I be correct in assuming that this is distinctly non-canon? It looked very much on theme/formatted similarly to V5, so I just sort of assumed it was a White Wolf official book","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25663-rigelj","name":"RigelJ","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T10:22:17-08:00","id":1346499,"title":"","content":"Ask away! That said, I specifically didn't convert over every brithright, frailty, or art. The purpose of the conversion guide is to provide a broad framework and a starting point. I don't want to tread on White Wolf, Onyx Path, or Modiphius, so I don't want to negate the need for copies of C20 and V5.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RigelJ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1340810-c5-ruminations?p=1346492#post1346492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">also, would I be correct in assuming that this is distinctly non-canon?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, this is purely a fan work, despite being done by someone's who's worked on the C20 line. It does my tip hand a bit with what I was thinking whenever I wrote about Nightmare and the Thallain, but even that's not official. The line developer would decide what the truth is should it ever be revealed.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T10:46:49-08:00","id":1346505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1340810-c5-ruminations?p=1346499#post1346499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ask away! That said, I specifically didn't convert over every brithright, frailty, or art. The purpose of the conversion guide is to provide a broad framework and a starting point. I don't want to tread on White Wolf, Onyx Path, or Modiphius, so I don't want to negate the need for copies of C20 and V5.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>1. Legacies here are a touch confusing. You say each Changeling has 3, is that to say they have the regular C20 ones and ALSO the ones provided here? How do they work in concert/conflict? How does one heal Willpower Agg. Normally a Changeling manifests one as a primary and the other as a secondary. How does this fit into that equation?<br /> <br /> 2. You described how banality &quot;Stains&quot; work as such: &quot;A character gains a point of Banality when the mundane takes priority over her role as a being of myth and legend: when either a chronicle tenant or one of the character\u2019s bans is breached.&quot;<br /> <br /> However, you dont include things such as microaggressions as mentioned above. Would it be fair to say flagrant demonstrations of Changeling nature, like using Wyrd Magic at the grocery store would incur stains? Or would you just assume that this would be addressed within the confines of the Chronicle Tenants? It seemed like you were suggesting that Banality came exclusively from intentional breaking of rules, but maybe I just dont have a great grasp on the breadth of what chronicle tenants can include","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25663,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25663-rigelj","user":"RigelJ","date":". 11-06-2019, 02:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25663-rigelj","name":"RigelJ","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T11:23:30-08:00","id":1346520,"title":"","content":"Do you mean Quests? Because yes, changelings get 3 \u2014 one from the Legacy and two chosen by the player. One player chosen Quest is a long term Quest that behaves exactly like Ambitions in V5 and the other is a short term one that works exactly like V5's Desire.<br /> <br /> Legacies in and of themselves work nothing like in C20, despite the reuse of the name. In this, they're the broad faerie types, analogous to Kiths in C20. In this, Kiths are just a subset of Legacies. In fact, if I were doing this as a new edition instead of a conversion guide, I'd probably go farther and only have the Kiths provide a single Birthright with everything else coming from the Legacy.<br /> <br /> Aggravated Willpower damage is healed exactly as it is in V5, just swap out &quot;long term Quest&quot; for Ambition.<br /> <br /> Banality is gained similarly to Stains in V5 \u2014 through Chronicle Tenants and the character's Bans. They can be crafted so that you have a wide range of options that can be tailored to the troupe's preferences. Unleashing the Wyrd in a grocery store, by default, doesn't automatically confer Banality. It does, however, carry enough danger otherwise from Nightmare, the Darkening, and attracting the attention of the changeling's enemies, that Unleashing frivolously probably isn't a wise course of action.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T12:58:00-08:00","id":1346549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1340810-c5-ruminations?p=1346520#post1346520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Legacies in and of themselves work nothing like in C20, despite the reuse of the name. In this, they're the broad faerie types, analogous to Kiths in C20. In this, Kiths are just a subset of Legacies. In fact, if I were doing this as a new edition instead of a conversion guide, I'd probably go farther and only have the Kiths provide a single Birthright with everything else coming from the Legacy.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>were on the same wavelength now.<br /> <br /> Okay cool! My last question (for now) is about the Tithed. This was perhaps one of the coolest concepts in the book, simply because it gets right to the worst parts of what a changeling is and slaps them in the face with it (possibly with multiple tithed for a single Changeling, depending on how many times they have reincarnated). However, it was only like a paragraph!<br /> <br /> &quot;The Tithed have a spiritual connection to their changeling, allowing them to slip right into her mortal Seeming while the changeling is otherwise occupied.&quot;<br /> <br /> Define &quot;otherwise occupied&quot;. Is there something that Changelings can do to ensure the Tithed don't just take back their rightful bodies? Are the Tithed purely chimerical while they're not in a human body, or can humans see them? Does Banality hurt them too? How long can they take back their body? Or are they more &quot;evil twin&quot; with bodies only when they want to be seen by people, and they just make an Autumn body seemingly from nothing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25663,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25663-rigelj","user":"RigelJ","date":". 11-06-2019, 08:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25663-rigelj","name":"RigelJ","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T13:24:34-08:00","id":1346557,"title":"","content":"I can't take credit for the Tithed. They're originally from the Time of Judgement book, and as far as I know, were created by Pete Woodworth. I've always thought they're cool villains and figured this was a good place to reintroduce them.<br /> <br /> In this case, it just means the changeling isn't paying attention to mundane concerns. It gives the evil twin a chance to step in and ruin the mundane side of the changeling's life. Thanks to Wyrd-ness of the Dreaming, the Tithed have a body, they just don't have a life to come back to (it got stolen by the changeling). The Wyrd is always susceptible to Banality \u2014 the Tithed, Fell, and Branded are no exceptions. Their Bans are probably a bit different than your average changeling's though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T17:18:22-08:00","id":1346621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1340810-c5-ruminations?p=1346557#post1346557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't take credit for the Tithed. They're originally from the Time of Judgement book, and as far as I know, were created by Pete Woodworth. I've always thought they're cool villains and figured this was a good place to reintroduce them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Time of Judgement huh? Im newer to the canon, and basically only own a changeling book if its under your handle (or is Kithbook Boggans), so I'll have to dig for a copy. They sound cool, but I def need a little bit more juice before theyre playable bad guys. Im a fan of making bad guys that don't follow conventional rules for players, but I want them to have internal rules that THEY follow. Makes it seem less slipshod and like Im just doing whatever I want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25663-rigelj","name":"RigelJ","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T03:28:32-08:00","id":1346689,"title":"","content":"My suggestion for a fourth Changeling (taking into account it sounds kind of daunting to think about making a fourth Changeling), would be to make it much less USAcentric. Specially the differing treatment in quantity to different parts of the world is kind of weird, and the part on several kingdoms of Europe seems off to me (unless divorce from historical/cultural reality is intended? I'm talking about C20 specifically). Also I think having those kiths relegated to an appendix is weird, I would put them all together. Maybe classify them on regions, plus a guide on making kiths. As for rules, I have no idea really. I imagine they're already gonna import stuff like Touchstones from CoD anyways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25136-kev\u00e4\u00e4n-neito","name":"Kev\u00e4\u00e4n Neito","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25136_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T09:37:11-08:00","id":1346750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kev\u00e4\u00e4n Neito</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1340810-c5-ruminations?p=1346689#post1346689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My suggestion for a fourth Changeling (taking into account it sounds kind of daunting to think about making a fourth Changeling), would be to make it much less USAcentric. Specially the differing treatment in quantity to different parts of the world is kind of weird, and the part on several kingdoms of Europe seems off to me (unless divorce from historical/cultural reality is intended? I'm talking about C20 specifically). Also I think having those kiths relegated to an appendix is weird, I would put them all together. Maybe classify them on regions, plus a guide on making kiths. As for rules, I have no idea really. I imagine they're already gonna import stuff like Touchstones from CoD anyways.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some of this is in part a result of C20 being a 'nostalgia edition'.<br /> <br /> Much of the info on European kingdoms is based on earlier editions' European work (Isle of the Mighty for the UK, Court of All Kings for Ireland, and The Fools' Luck for mainland Europe) without a significant overhaul, mainly filling in the spots they didn't cover.<br /> <br /> Since previous focus was on the Western Kithain as main splats in the Changeling cores, they kept that for C20, folding in the other Kithain introduced during the line, and following in V20 and W20's footsteps by having the other splats introduced during the run in the back. (M20's example, with the Technocracy and Disparates, suggests there could have been other options.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T09:44:36-08:00","id":1346755,"title":"","content":"The Players Guide has a lot of stuff on non-European kiths. Also the Swan Maidens (my personal fave).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T10:25:51-08:00","id":1346766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1340810-c5-ruminations?p=1346750#post1346750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(M20's example, with the Technocracy and Disparates, suggests there could have been other options.)</div> </div> </div> </div>From what I understand, that was an active decision on Brucato's part to break away from the mold of the WoD20a corebooks. And not a mandate from OPP.<br /> <br /> I suspect that's why C20 and Wr20 were formatted the way they were: the devs decided to just continue using the format established by V20 and W20.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T16:28:51-08:00","id":1346891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1340810-c5-ruminations?p=1346750#post1346750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.<br /> <br /> Since previous focus was on the Western Kithain as main splats in the Changeling cores, they kept that for C20, folding in the other Kithain introduced during the line, and following in V20 and W20's footsteps by having the other splats introduced during the run in the back. (M20's example, with the Technocracy and Disparates, suggests there could have been other options.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Mage doesn't have things that completely follow theirown rules.. a Technocrat more or less follows the same mechanics as a Tradition or Disparate so its much easier to just slide them in. inanimae and Hsien are using vastly different mechanics enough that they had separte books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T03:58:10-08:00","id":1347852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1340810-c5-ruminations?p=1346755#post1346755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Players Guide has a lot of stuff on non-European kiths. Also the Swan Maidens (my personal fave).</div> </div> </div> </div>I want this book but I don't have it yet!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25136-kev\u00e4\u00e4n-neito","name":"Kev\u00e4\u00e4n Neito","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25136_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T05:43:39-08:00","id":1347869,"title":"","content":"Defo worth buying","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T08:34:02-08:00","id":1347910,"title":"","content":"I certainly think it's a worthwhile purchase, but I may be a little biased <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-20T02:20:34-08:00","id":1349817,"title":"","content":"I'm amazed and delighted at seeing this, this feels like a massive realization of ideas that changeling has been grasping at but hasn't been quite ready to commit to and a step towards bringing out the horror in the setting it wasn't quite able to embrace. Like Rise of the Guardians if it was done by Niel Gaiman. I'm in love with the direction this is taking and would be overjoyed to see this reach the point where it didn't require c20 to use so that is could stand without needing the older editions to hold it up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","name":"Darkfoxdev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-20T09:06:45-08:00","id":1349866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1340810-c5-ruminations?p=1347910#post1347910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I certainly think it's a worthwhile purchase, but I may be a little biased <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So now that I've gotten myself mega hyped to try this format of play... Is there a character sheet somewhere? Editing PDF's isn't really my strong suit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25663-rigelj","name":"RigelJ","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-21T16:16:48-08:00","id":1350145,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar648_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"648\" data-vbnamecard=\"648\">PookaKnight</a> I just want to say I really love the merger of actor and fae into a new form of actor, and I <i><b>really </b></i>love the new requirements at each level, it very much suits how I like to play fae magic. With that in mind I do feel the need to ask; how do the fae affect themselves (that is, the caster not all kithain) with the new actor realm? They can't use fae 1-2 anymore so presumably they'd need to reach actor 3 and use their own name, but that seems a little much for a self-empowerment, should being able to effect yourself be a secondary effect of actor 1 or is needing actor 3 the intention.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","name":"Darkfoxdev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-21T16:42:35-08:00","id":1350150,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3729\" data-vbnamecard=\"3729\">Darkfoxdev</a> Good catch. Yeah, it\u2019s Actor 1. I should have made a note about it, but I just didn\u2019t think about it.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25663-rigelj\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25663\" data-vbnamecard=\"25663\">RigelJ</a> I probably should have made a character sheet to go with it. I\u2019ll see if I can whip something up after I get over this bout of sickness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-21T17:51:19-08:00","id":1350156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkfoxdev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1340810-c5-ruminations?p=1350145#post1350145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar648_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"648\" data-vbnamecard=\"648\">PookaKnight</a> I just want to say I really love the merger of actor and fae into a new form of actor, and I <i><b>really </b></i>love the new requirements at each level, it very much suits how I like to play fae magic. With that in mind I do feel the need to ask; how do the fae affect themselves (that is, the caster not all kithain) with the new actor realm? They can't use fae 1-2 anymore so presumably they'd need to reach actor 3 and use their own name, but that seems a little much for a self-empowerment, should being able to effect yourself be a secondary effect of actor 1 or is needing actor 3 the intention.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You don't need fae 1/2 to self target you can always self target by c20 rules. YOu need fae 1/2 ot target your friends.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-21T18:10:36-08:00","id":1350158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1340810-c5-ruminations?p=1350156#post1350156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You don't need fae 1/2 to self target you can always self target by c20 rules. YOu need fae 1/2 ot target your friends.</div> </div> </div> </div>I must have missed that, in fact two of the examples explicitely cite the user needing fae 1 to target themselves in both the realms explanation and the <i>seven dreams brought to lif</i>e. Do you know which page that's on?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","name":"Darkfoxdev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-28T06:43:22-08:00","id":1351466,"title":"","content":"I really like this, but I wouldn't play it. Like V5, it feels like a 'lite' version of the game (not just rules-wise). I miss that depth. But this would be great for a non-CTD game about modern faeries, and is a breezy read. Thanks so much for making it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-01T07:04:37-08:00","id":1352008,"title":"","content":"Likewise. There isn't much there that would draw interest in shifting over, and I am currently more interested in seeing C20 fleshed out more before it jumps to a new system altogether.<br /> <br /> I can &quot;understand&quot; the idea between wanting to disassociate Fae, since it tends to act as a wildcard for &quot;things of the Dreaming,&quot; whether Nature, Chimera, Chimerical items, etc. <br /> <br /> However, even with the assorted Arts, the Actor 5 stipulation preventing &quot;Blind aiming&quot; of cantrips, combined with the esoteric nature of certain object options (e.x. would you consider &quot;network packets&quot; or &quot;soundwaves&quot; a variant of Prop or Naturel) means that even assuming you hypothetically have maxed out Realms, there are some things you Just Cannot Do.<br /> <br /> Another option could be to make Fae a &quot;modifier&quot; realm, similar to Time or Scene. Lower levels allow for abilities to target chimera or ephemera, or to use a &quot;single&quot; realm to manipulate concepts which ambiguously fall in an unknown Realm. Mid-level ones allow for metamagic-mutability of certain Cantrips, &quot;Spell completion&quot; Bunks (e.x. a Scroll of Wayfare&quot;, &quot;wildcard/probabilistic&quot; targeting when combined with Time, or manipulation of Oaths.<br /> <br /> This would grant it a distinct purpose over the three &quot;base&quot; realms which are variants of &quot;person/place/thing.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25625-magicjuggler","name":"MagicJuggler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25625_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-01T13:55:21-08:00","id":1352051,"title":"","content":"Victor and Simon invited me back to Walking Away From Arcadia to talk about my 5th edition World of Darkness conversion guide for Changeling: The Dreaming. As always, they were a joy to chat with. I hope folks enjoy our discussion!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://walkingawayfromarcadia.podbean.com/e/5th-edition-conversion-guide-with-charlie/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://pbcdn1.podbean.com/fs1/site/images/logo-im